Description: open-source video editor
 FilmCraft is a native, nonlinear video editor written in Rust. It has timeline
 editing with source and program monitors, colour grading and scopes, effects
 and keyframes, titles and captions, audio mixing with loudness meters and
 export, and it composites on the GPU (wgpu).
 .
 The headless command runner, exporter and MCP server that drive the same
 editor commands are in the storytold-filmcraft-cli package.

Package: storytold-filmcraft-cli
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Suggests: storytold-filmcraft (= ${binary:Version}),
         storytold-craft-fonts,
Enhances: storytold-filmcraft,
Description: headless command runner, exporter and MCP server for the FilmCraft editor
 filmcraft-cli runs FilmCraft's editor commands without a window: it opens a
 project or starts an empty one, runs commands from a list or a script, probes
 media files, renders frames and exports the active sequence.
 .
 filmcraft-cli mcp starts an MCP server on standard input and output, so that
 an AI agent can drive the editor engine, headless or attached to a running
 FilmCraft window. It has no windowing or GPU dependencies. The
 storytold-filmcraft package provides the editor window.
